          "filename": "Santa Barbara County Courthouse.jpg",
          "caption": "NO. 1037 Santa Barbara County Courthouse - The Santa Barbara County Courthouse was constructed in 1929 and is a complex of four buildings occupying an entire city block in downtown Santa Barbara.  It was designed by master architect William Mooser in the Spanish Colonial/Moorish Revival style.  It is an extraordinary example of its style, with an elaborate array of detail emulating a Spanish castle or fortress. \n\nLocation:  1100 Anacapa Street, Santa Barbara",
